    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** enter today\u2019s slate with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (78.75) and **Kyle Tucker** (77.19) anchoring the lineup, both benefiting from highly favorable matchups. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** draws a prime spot against Basso, where a combination of park factors and a strong platoon edge solidify him as our highest-upside play. Meanwhile, **Kyle Tucker** continues to provide elite efficiency against the suboptimal arm of Rhett Lowder. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** also projects as a high-tier asset today (74.55); his massive 19% SP Skill advantage against Tomoyuki Sugano, compounded by an excellent dynamic platoon split, makes him a must-start despite the speculative lineup placement.\n\nWe are navigating a few tactical tradeoffs today, most notably with **Nasim Nunez** (52.32), who remains in the lineup despite a lower raw score to protect our stolen base equity. His utility is preserved even against a tough arm like Walker Buehler due to his profile as an elite speed generator. The closest call on the bench was **Miguel Vargas** (49.54); while he carries a respectable xwOBA of 0.385 and benefits from a favorable SP delivery profile, the optimizer opted for **Sam Antonacci** (51.77) at the bottom of the OF rotation, banking on the significant +10% boost from the leadoff spot to edge out **Miguel Vargas**'s marginal output.\n\nRisk management remains a primary focus, as several key slots for **Liam Hicks**, **Drake Baldwin**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Coby Mayo**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Sam Antonacci**, and **Kyle Tucker** currently depend on \"Lineup Pending\" status. While **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo** benefit significantly from wind-out conditions and positive park factors, their reliance on projected orders introduces volatility. We are monitoring the weather closely; should any late lineup shifts move our core speed threats out of favorable table-setting positions, we will re-evaluate our pinch-hit aggression to ensure we do not waste game caps on sub-optimal efficiency.",
